# Electron Main + IPC

## IPC naming

Use `domain:action` channels: `settings:get`, `settings:set`, `readiness:scan`, `dialog:pickDir`, `shell:openPath`, `job:run`, `job:cancel`.

Streaming events (main → renderer): `job:started`, `job:log`, `job:ended`.

## Adding a feature (4-file pattern)

1. Type in `src/shared/types.ts`
2. Logic in `src/main/<domain>.ts`
3. `ipcMain.handle(...)` in `src/main/index.ts`
4. Method on `api` in `src/preload/index.ts` (types flow via `WindowApi` / `preload/index.d.ts`)

## Jobs

- `job:run` returns immediately with `{ id, commandPreview }`; work runs async
- Stream logs via `sender.send('job:log', ...)` and finish with `job:ended`
- Use `ProcessController` from `process.ts` for spawn/cancel
- Throw `JobCancelledError` when user cancels
- Only one `activeJob` — reject or queue if another is running

## Security

- No secrets in `settings.ts` / `settings.json`
- Validate DB names before embedding in SQL (`databases.ts`)
- Keep `contextIsolation: true`, `nodeIntegration: false` in BrowserWindow

## Platform

- Linux: `no-sandbox` already set in `index.ts`
- Optional GPU disable: `SSHR_DB_SUITE_DISABLE_GPU=1`
- Packaged backup dir: `~/Documents/SSHR Database Suite/db_backups` (see `paths.ts`)

## Do not

- Add `.sh` scripts — TypeScript orchestration only
- Put `fs`, `child_process`, or `ipcRenderer` in renderer code
- Block `ipcMain.handle` on long-running CLI work

## Auto-updates

- Logic in `updater.ts`; started from `index.ts` after window create
- IPC: `update:check`, `update:install`, event `update:status`
- Packaged AppImage only; GitHub Releases via `build.publish`
